"Gh05t-1337","id":95411780,"node_id":"U_kgDOBa_eRA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95411780?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gh05t-1337","html_url":"https://github.com/Gh05t-1337","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gh05t-1337/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gh05t-1337/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gh05t-1337/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gh05t-1337/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gh05t-1337/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gh05t-1337/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gh05t-1337/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gh05t-1337/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gh05t-1337/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-19T00:14:19Z","updated_at":"2025-02-19T00:14:19Z","body":"small update: if i do the position.x = 10 in the characterbody's _init function instead, it doesnt collide anymore, it works as intended. still weird that it has a problem when i do it on_ready, while no other physics body has that problem","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2667208209/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2667461834","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102971#issuecomment-2667461834","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102971","id":2667461834,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6e_jzK","user":{"login":"M4t1c","id":197941145,"node_id":"U_kgDOC8xXmQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/197941145?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/M4t1c","html_url":"https://github.com/M4t1c","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/M4t1c/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/M4t1c/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/M4t1c/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/M4t1c/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/M4t1c/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/M4t1c/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/M4t1c/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/M4t1c/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/M4t1c/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-19T04:08:34Z","updated_at":"2025-02-19T04:08:34Z","body":"I believe I have a similar issue and came here looking to see if anyone else also has it. If it is different please tell me and I will create a separate issue.\n\nTL;DR: If I remove and add a CharacterBody2D parent node with remove_child and add_child, collision triggers even though right before calling remove_child CharacterBody2D was moved outside of the collision (If I just remove calls to remove_child and add_child collision does not trigger).\n\nHere is my Godot Forum post that explains it in more detail: https://forum.godotengine.org/t/interesting-collision-behavior-when-removing-and-adding-nodes-to-the-scene-tree/102235?u=m4tic\n\nSystem: Godot v4.3.stable - Windows 10.0.26100 - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 Ti Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-12900H (20 Threads)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2667461834/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692402465","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102971#issuecomment-2692402465","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102971","id":2692402465,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ges0h","user":{"login":"adam-stone","id":16766925,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzY2OTI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16766925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adam-stone","html_url":"https://github.com/adam-stone","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adam-stone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adam-stone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adam-stone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adam-stone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adam-stone/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adam-stone/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adam-stone/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adam-stone/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adam-stone/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-01T20:26:24Z","updated_at":"2025-03-01T20:26:24Z","body":"Also seeing this issue in the following environment:\n\nGodot v4.3.stable - macOS 15.3.1 - GLES3 (Compatibility) - Apple M2 Pro - Apple M2 Pro (12 Threads)\n\nAs with previous reporters, what I'm seeing is that a character body (my example is 2D) that has been removed from the scene and re-added triggers an area's on_body_entered signal even though it is no longer in that area. A couple of notes from my testing:\n- I do not observe the issue if I replace the character body with a rigid body. The exact same code for removing and re-adding the rigid body does not cause the spurious `on_body_entered` signal.\n- The character body only causes the incorrect `on_body_entered` signal the first time it is re-added to the scene. That is, the character body enters the area and is removed from the scene. It is assigned a new position outside of the area and re-added to the scene, and `on_body_entered` gets emitted again. If I add the character body back to the scene again at the same location, the area does not fire its signal.\n- I've tried changing the body position both before and after the `remove_child` call, and all `remove_child` and `add_child` calls are deferred.\n\n[characterbody-collide-mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19040593/characterbody-collide-mrp.zip)\n\n(Probably obvious from looking at the script, but the MRP uses a keypress to trigger respawn and assumes that you have move_* input bindings to move the character body.)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692402465/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3035774903","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102971#issuecomment-3035774903","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102971","id":3035774903,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc608j-3","user":{"login":"M4t1c","id":197941145,"node_id":"U_kgDOC8xXmQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/197941145?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/M4t1c","html_url":"https://github.com/M4t1c","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/M4t1c/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/M4t1c/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/M4t1c/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/M4t1c/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/M4t1c/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/M4t1c/orgs","repos_url":"